WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.860
Speaker 1: Well, COVID quarantine has been
an extraordinary productive period for President

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:06.860
Joe Biden.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:08.059
And I'm not kidding around.

00:00:08.059 --> 00:00:13.230
I mean, think back to when Donald Trump had
COVID and he was stuck in a hospital at one

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:21.140
point receiving supplemental oxygen, sending
lie laced tweets at the time, going out and

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:25.830
exposing his Secret Service detail to COVID
when he made them drive him around the block

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:26.830
in his SUV.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:31.630
I mean, just a pathetically globally humiliating
COVID period for Donald Trump.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:35.400
We can't even really call it COVID quarantine
because he wasn't properly isolating.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:41.230
Joe Biden, on the other hand, we already knew
had overseen and authorized the killing of

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:43.910
al Qaeda terrorist Ayman al-Zawahiri.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:47.700
Legitimate questions about the legal framework
for these killings.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:53.579
You know, I'm right there with you, but an
accomplishment by international standards,

00:00:53.579 --> 00:00:59.780
an extraordinarily strong jobs report late
last week, which we will get to later.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:00.780
But the big news.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:03.809
Oh, and gas prices declining 54 days in a
row.

00:01:03.809 --> 00:01:07.090
And I'm kind of kidding because, as you know,
I don't actually think presidents have much

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:11.150
to do with gas prices, but by their standards,
another accomplishment.

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:16.760
And now the really, really big news over the
weekend, the Senate approving a bill to fight

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:22.440
climate change and cut drug costs, not insulin,
unfortunately, thanks to Republicans.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:24.200
But we will get to that as well.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:30.720
But we are really racking up major accomplishments
here for Joe Biden and it couldn't come as

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.700
a better time as Democrats are surging in
midterm election polls.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:41.500
Tomorrow, we will talk about could this be
one of the worst midterms for Republicans

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.909
after a Democrat takes the White House?

00:01:43.909 --> 00:01:47.220
The answer is yes, it could be, but we will
get to that tomorrow.

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:56.780
Reuters reporting the U.S. Senate Sunday passed
a sweeping $430 billion bill intended to fight

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:58.080
climate change.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:05.479
Lower drug prices raise some corporate taxes
in a major victory for Joe Biden, which Democrats

00:02:05.479 --> 00:02:12.430
hope will help them in November after a marathon
27 hour weekend session of debate and Republican

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:17.610
efforts to derail the package, the Senate
approved the legislation known as the Inflation

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:20.550
Reduction Act by a 51 to 50 party line vote.

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:24.520
Vice President Kamala Harris cast the tiebreaking
ballot.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:29.370
This sends the measure to the House of Representatives
for a vote probably Friday.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:33.720
They're expected to pass it, send it to the
White House for Joe Biden's signature.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:38.870
The Senate is making history, said an elated
Senate Majority Leader, Chuck Schumer.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:43.960
To Americans who have lost faith that Congress
can do big things, this bill is for you.

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:48.070
Schumer says the legislation contains the
boldest clean energy package in American history

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:55.040
to fight climate change while reducing consumer
costs for energy and some medicines.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:58.790
The legislation is aimed at reducing carbon
emissions and shifting consumers to green

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:02.820
energy, cutting prescription drug costs for
the elderly, and tightening enforcement on

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:05.610
taxes for corporations and the wealthy.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:11.400
The measure pays for itself and reduces the
federal deficit over time.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:14.750
Democrats contend it will help down bring
down inflation.

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:21.350
Economists have, generally speaking, agreed
with that from the Washington Post.

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:25.780
Senate Approves Inflation Reduction Act Clinching
Long Delayed Health and Climate Bill.

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:30.230
The party line vote marks a major achievement
for Democrats after more than a year of wrangling

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:34.190
over the centerpiece of President Biden's
economic agenda.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:37.590
This is a really, really big deal.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:44.190
And zoom out for a moment and think about
the last two weeks for Joe Biden, understanding

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:51.431
that I am giving you a public analysis, understanding,
as you and I have talked about before, that

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:55.670
not all of the things I'm about to mention
directly relate to Joe Biden.

00:03:55.670 --> 00:04:01.840
We have essentially full employment right
now, more than 500,000 new jobs in the latest

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.500
job jobs report.

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:06.150
Unemployment down to 3.5%.

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:12.530
This is an extraordinary jobs report, an unemployment
situation by any measure.

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:15.880
Ayman al Zawahiri, major Al Qaida terrorist
killed.

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:17.760
Now, we might say that was illegal.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:18.760
Okay.

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:19.950
Well, I'm not disagreeing with that.

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:24.660
But from the point of view of the accomplishments
Biden can now claim in terms of saying reward

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:32.580
Democrats in November, Inflation Reduction
Act, with major advances in a number of different

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.270
areas, doing a number of good things.

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:38.460
And, by the way, expected to push down inflation,
which I believe tomorrow.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:39.960
Tomorrow we are get it or no?

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:43.300
On Wednesday we are getting the July inflation
numbers.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:48.700
I believe they are going to look much better
and I believe it is going to bump up the market,

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:49.700
etc..

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:53.050
And now in addition, gas prices coming down
about 20%.

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:54.490
I mean, again, it's sort of a joke.

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:58.150
I don't think Biden had anything to do with
them going up nor coming down.

00:04:58.150 --> 00:04:59.150
But when we say it's.

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:00.150
The economy, stupid.

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:03.200
And people look at certain indicators to determine
are things going well?

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.950
They're not going well.

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:07.410
That's one of the things that they look at
now.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:14.330
Fox News and right wing media are calling
this bill a social bill spending spree as

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:19.710
if health care is some kind of frivolous pet
project or social issue.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:23.930
When it's not like it's going to be for gay
marriage or who the hell knows what.

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:27.030
Republicans are saying Democrats are going
to pay the price for this bill.

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:30.590
I don't believe that that's the case, but
we will know in under three months.

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:32.250
Now, one other thing.

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:34.900
Diabetics should remember when it's time to
vote.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:39.400
And really, everybody should remember that
one of the amendments that Republican senators

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:44.440
killed was a $35 cap on insulin.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:50.590
Senate Republicans yesterday stripped a proposed
$35 a month cap on out-of-pocket spending

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:54.630
on insulin for patients enrolled in private
insurance.

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:59.721
The Senate parliamentarian earlier ruled the
provision is not primarily related to the

00:05:59.721 --> 00:06:03.400
federal budget, so it's not eligible to be
passed by 50 votes.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.050
They needed 60 votes.

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:07.350
Only seven Republicans voted for it.

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:12.190
So the insulin amendment failed by three votes.

00:06:12.190 --> 00:06:13.450
These people are disgusting.

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:14.940
They truly are.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:16.590
And we will see in November.

